# Canonical pins for this repo's Dockerfile. Bump via scripts/bump-pin.sh.
# Last updated: 2026-05-06 (Wave 10: full cu13 stack migration)
DEEPEP_FORK=https://github.com/dmvevents/DeepEP-1.git
DEEPEP_BRANCH=aws-efa-auto-qp-cap-v2
DEEPEP_SHA=146cc356aa00c39ac1590c05775e05b0f031e70c

# Wave 10: unified cu13 stack to resolve Wave 9c finding that cu12 NCCL
# wheels do NOT expose the DeepEP V2 GIN ABI (ncclTeamWorld,
# ncclCommProperties, etc.) that csrc/kernels/backend/nccl.cu calls.
# cu13 NCCL wheels DO expose those symbols, and cu13 also resolves
# Wave 8's invalid-device-ordinal crash caused by two libcudart.so
# copies (torch cu12 + vllm _C.abi3.so cu13) racing on TLS.
#
# Per god-mode 3-model consensus 2026-05-06 (Option 3: flip every
# runtime component to cu13). Build OS remains cu12.9-devel because
# nvidia/cuda:13.0-devel-ubuntu24.04 is not yet on Docker Hub
# (verified 2026-05-06); cu13 runtime components land via pip wheels.
#
# NOTE: the value MUST be single-quoted because `>=` would otherwise
# be interpreted as shell redirection when pins.env is sourced
# (regression seen in a failed v0.1.2-sm90a GHA run).
NVIDIA_NCCL_PIN='nvidia-nccl-cu13>=2.30.4'

# PyTorch index URL (cu130 wheel). Stable cu130 torch is 2.11.0+cu130
# (verified via `pip index versions torch --index-url
# https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130` 2026-05-06). The Dockerfile
# pins to 2.11.0+cu130 explicitly to avoid silent ABI drift.
TORCH_INDEX=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130
